LAMMPS (22 Jul 2025 - Update 2)
KOKKOS mode with Kokkos version 4.6.2 is enabled
  will use up to 1 GPU(s) per node
WARNING: When using a single thread, the Kokkos Serial backend (i.e. Makefile.kokkos_mpi_only) gives better performance than the OpenMP backend (src/KOKKOS/kokkos.cpp:221)
  using 1 OpenMP thread(s) per MPI task
package kokkos
package kokkos neigh half newton on
# =============================================================================
# LAMMPS input script for PDMS melt-quench densification
# =============================================================================
# Purpose: Achieve target density ~1.10 g/cm^3 for crosslinked PDMS
#
# Workflow:
#   1. Energy minimization
#   2. Heat from 300K to 443K (170C, curing temperature)
#   3. NPT equilibration at 443K (high temperature relaxation)
#   4. Cool down from 443K to 300K
#   5. Final NPT equilibration at 300K
#   6. Output densified structure
#
# Chemistry context:
#   - Curing agent: 2,5-dimethyl-2,5-di(tert-butylperoxy)hexane (1%)
#   - Curing conditions: 170C (443K), 10 min
#   - Target density: 1.10 g/cm^3
# =============================================================================

log             melt_quench_log.lammps
